    "title": "17. Transformer Protection Schemes",
    "preview": "A transformer is protected by layered electrical relays plus its own mechanical devices (§7.4). The aim: clear internal faults in &lt; 100 ms (every extra cycle of arcing multiplies the damage and the oil-fire risk) while never tripping on inrush, OLTC operation or through-faults.",
